findings

  FINDING the endpoint delivered 480 frames per packet at p50 and the encoder took 240 of them per frame, so one packet became 2 datagrams of 81 bytes
  FINDING 148.8 kbps on the wire including RTP headers, at 200.00 datagrams a second
  FINDING the sending thread ran as MMCSS Pro Audio, thread priority 18

what must not be zero

  PASS  packets came off the endpoint            15000
        every count and every percentile in this document is taken over these packets, so a run that collected none makes each of them an absence rather than a number, and loopback delivers nothing at all while the endpoint is idle
  PASS  datagrams went onto the wire             30000
        the receiving end's loss figure is a fraction of what this end sent, and a sender that sent nothing makes a receiver that received nothing look like a radio that lost everything

what must be zero

  PASS  no packet left a residue                 0 over 15000 capture_packets
        there is no accumulator on this path because A1 measured that there is never a residue, so a residue is a finding about the endpoint rather than a tolerance; the population is the packets, because no packets leave nothing over just as convincingly
  PASS  the socket refused nothing               0 over 30000 frames_encoded
        a refused send is this host's own doing rather than the link's, and a run with any of them is measuring a machine that could not keep the socket fed; the population is the frames encoded, because nothing offered is never refused
  PASS  no frames missing from the device position 0 over 7200000 capture_frames
        the device position of a packet must equal the previous position plus the previous frame count, so a gap is audio the engine could not hand over and its size is known exactly; the population is the frames captured, because a stream that delivered none has no holes in it
  PASS  the device position never went backwards 0 over 15000 capture_packets
        a hole is audio that was lost and a rewind is a position stream that cannot be trusted at all, so they are counted apart and this one is not a tolerance

what else must hold

  PASS  every captured sample was encoded        7200000 against 7200000 samples_captured
        a 5 ms frame is 240 samples and the endpoint delivers exactly two frames' worth in every packet, so the split is exact or it is not a split; the two counts agreeing is the proof, and audio lost here cannot be told apart by a receiver from audio lost on the air
  PASS  every encoded frame became a datagram    30000 against 30000 frames_encoded
        one Opus frame is one datagram in this payload format, so the two counts are the same measurement taken at two boundaries, and a shortfall is a frame the socket refused rather than a frame the radio lost
  PASS  the timestamp advanced by the frame's samples every time 30000 against 30000 timestamp_steps
        the RTP timestamp is a sample counter, and one that drifted with this sender's scheduling would leave a receiver unable to tell a late packet from a packet describing a later moment
  PASS  encode p99 under a tenth of the frame    213 against a bound of 500
        a tenth of the 5 ms frame is 500 us, and an encoder under that cannot be the term that matters in a budget measured in whole milliseconds; p99 and not the mean, because a frame late once every hundred is a click a listener hears
  PASS  the endpoint carried the left channel's tone 997 against 997 give or take 5
        a packet count and a datagram count agree just as happily when the host was playing nothing, and a receiver that reports no underruns while playing silence has carried nothing either; 997 Hz comes out of the captured samples themselves
  PASS  the endpoint carried the right channel's tone 1997 against 1997 give or take 5
        the two channels carry different frequencies so that channel order is provable rather than assumed, and a right channel reading 997 Hz is what a fold to mono and a channel read twice both look like

PASS 12 of 12 checks hold and every declared subsystem was exercised
